From 50dbc2f0c9da14902afe3c1fe7ad5111ab2ca621 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:01:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): rest pass keeps corner reliefs on the rest center
 boundary

A 2D Pocket rest pass with a corner relief filtered the planned reliefs
with a bare point-in-region test on the rest center area. Each relief
start is a vertex of the pocket's center area, on the boundary of the
rest center area, so the test kept a relief by rounding: 1 of 4 dogbones
on a sharp 30 x 30 mm pocket.

The filter now tests the rest center area grown by 0.01 mm. A relief
that the rest pass does not keep gives a toolpath note.

Fixes #3146

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
